{"id":"mahabharata-7-041","work":"mahabharata","part":7,"partName":"द्रोणपर्व","partNameEn":"Drona Parva","unit":41,"title":"एकचत्वारिंशत्तमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 41 · Jayadratha's boon from Shiva","summary":{"en":"Dhritarashtra asks how the Kauravas could kill the young Abhimanyu. Sanjaya tells that Jayadratha, through a boon from Shiva, held back all the Pandavas but Arjuna for a day, so the Pandavas could not follow Abhimanyu into the array.","kn":"ಯುವ ಅಭಿಮನ್ಯುವನ್ನು ಕೌರವರು ಹೇಗೆ ಕೊಂದರೆಂದು ಧೃತರಾಷ್ಟ್ರ ಕೇಳುತ್ತಾನೆ. ಶಿವನ ವರದಿಂದ ಜಯದ್ರಥ ಅರ್ಜುನನ ಹೊರತು ಉಳಿದ ಪಾಂಡವರನ್ನು ಒಂದು ದಿನ ತಡೆದನೆಂದೂ ಹಾಗಾಗಿ ಅವರು ಅಭಿಮನ್ಯುವನ್ನು ಹಿಂಬಾಲಿಸಲಾಗಲಿಲ್ಲವೆಂದೂ ಸಂಜಯ ಹೇಳುತ್ತಾನೆ.","hi":"धृतराष्ट्र पूछते हैं कि कौरवों ने युवा अभिमन्यु को कैसे मारा। संजय बताते हैं कि शिव के वरदान से जयद्रथ ने अर्जुन के सिवा सब पाण्डवों को एक दिन रोके रखा, इसलिए वे अभिमन्यु के पीछे व्यूह में नहीं जा सके।","te":"యువ అభిమన్యుని కౌరవులు ఎలా చంపారని ధృతరాష్ట్రుడు అడుగుతాడు. శివుని వరం వల్ల జయద్రథుడు అర్జునుడు తప్ప మిగతా పాండవులను ఒక రోజు ఆపగా వారు అభిమన్యుని వెంట వ్యూహంలోకి వెళ్లలేకపోయారని సంజయుడు చెబుతాడు.","ta":"இளைய அபிமன்யுவைக் கௌரவர் எப்படிக் கொன்றனர் என்று த்ருதராஷ்டிரன் கேட்கிறான். சிவனின் வரத்தால் ஜயத்ரதன் அர்ஜுனனைத் தவிர மற்ற பாண்டவரை ஒரு நாள் தடுத்ததால், அவர்கள் அபிமன்யுவைப் பின்தொடர முடியவில்லை என்று சஞ்சயன் கூறுகிறான்.","ml":"ഈ ഇളംപ്രായക്കാരനായ അഭിമന്യുവിനെ കൗരവർ എങ്ങനെ കൊല്ലാനായെന്ന് ധൃതരാഷ്ട്രർ ചോദിക്കുന്നു. ശിവന്റെ വരത്താൽ ജയദ്രഥൻ ഒരു ദിവസം അർജുനനൊഴികെ എല്ലാ പാണ്ഡവരെയും തടഞ്ഞുനിർത്തിയെന്നും, അതിനാൽ അവർക്ക് വ്യൂഹത്തിനുള്ളിൽ അഭിമന്യുവിനെ പിന്തുടരാനായില്ലെന്നും സഞ്ജയൻ പറയുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 7.41; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Tue Sep 22 2026","sections":[{"title":"अभिमन्युवधपर्व","titleEn":"Abhimanyuvadha Parva (Slaying of Abhimanyu)","verses":[{"text":"धृतराष्ट्र उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Dhritarashtra said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"बालमत्यन्तसुखिनमवार्यबलदर्पितम् ।\nयुद्धेषु कुशलं वीरं कुलपुत्रं तनुत्यजम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"A boy living in great ease, proud of irresistible strength, a hero skilled in battle, of good family, ready to give up his body,"}},{"n":2,"text":"गाहमानमनीकानि सदश्वैस्तं त्रिहायनैः ।\nअपि यौधिष्ठिरात्सैन्यात्कश्चिदन्वपतद्रथी ॥","meaning":{"en":"plunging into armies with fine three-year-old horses: did any chariot-warrior of Yudhishthira's army follow him?"}},{"text":"संजय उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Sanjaya said:"}},{"n":3,"text":"युधिष्ठिरो भीमसेनः शिखण्डी सात्यकिर्यमौ ।\nधृष्टद्युम्नो विराटश्च द्रुपदश्च सकेकयः ।\nधृष्टकेतुश्च संरब्धो मत्स्याश्चान्वपतन्रणे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Yudhishthira, Bhimasena, Shikhandi, Satyaki, the twins, Dhrishtadyumna, Virata, Drupada with the Kekayas, and angry Dhrishtaketu and the Matsyas followed in the battle."}},{"n":4,"text":"अभ्यद्रवन्परीप्सन्तो व्यूढानीकाः प्रहारिणः ।\nतान्दृष्ट्वा द्रवतः शूरांस्त्वदीया विमुखाभवन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Eager to rescue him, those strikers rushed on with their divisions in array; seeing those brave men running, your men turned away."}},{"n":5,"text":"ततस्तद्विमुखं दृष्ट्वा तव सूनोर्महद्बलम् ।\nजामाता तव तेजस्वी विष्टम्भयिषुराद्रवत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, seeing your son's great army turned away, your son-in-law, the radiant Jayadratha, wishing to hold it firm, rushed forward."}},{"n":6,"text":"सैन्धवस्य महाराज पुत्रो राजा जयद्रथः ।\nस पुत्रगृद्धिनः पार्थान्सहसैन्यानवारयत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"He was King Jayadratha, son of the Sindhu king, O great king; he held back the Parthas with their armies, who were eager to save their son."}},{"n":7,"text":"उग्रधन्वा महेष्वासो दिव्यमस्त्रमुदीरयन् ।\nवार्धक्षत्रिरुपासेधत्प्रवणादिव कुञ्जरान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The strong archer Vriddhakshatra's son, calling up a divine weapon, held off the Pandavas like elephants held at a slope."}},{"text":"धृतराष्ट्र उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Dhritarashtra said:"}},{"n":8,"text":"अतिभारमहं मन्ये सैन्धवे संजयाहितम् ।\nयदेकः पाण्डवान्क्रुद्धान्पुत्रगृद्धीनवारयत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"I think, Sanjaya, too heavy a burden was laid on the Sindhu king, since he alone held back the angry Pandavas who were eager to save their son."}},{"n":9,"text":"अत्यद्भुतमिदं मन्ये बलं शौर्यं च सैन्धवे ।\nतदस्य ब्रूहि मे वीर्यं कर्म चाग्र्यं महात्मनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"I think this strength and valor of the Sindhu king is most marvelous; tell me his strength and his best deed, great-souled as he is."}},{"n":10,"text":"किं दत्तं हुतमिष्टं वा सुतप्तमथ वा तपः ।\nसिन्धुराजेन येनैकः क्रुद्धान्पार्थानवारयत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"What did the Sindhu king give, offer in sacrifice, or what austerity did he perform well, by which he alone held back the angry Parthas?"}},{"text":"संजय उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Sanjaya said:"}},{"n":11,"text":"द्रौपदीहरणे यत्तद्भीमसेनेन निर्जितः ।\nमानात्स तप्तवान्राजा वरार्थी सुमहत्तपः ॥","meaning":{"en":"When he was defeated by Bhimasena at the carrying off of Draupadi, the king, in pride, wishing for a boon, performed great austerity."}},{"n":12,"text":"इन्द्रियाणीन्द्रियार्थेभ्यः प्रियेभ्यः संनिवर्त्य सः ।\nक्षुत्पिपासातपसहः कृशो धमनिसंततः ।\nदेवमाराधयच्छर्वं गृणन्ब्रह्म सनातनम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Withdrawing his senses from their pleasing objects, bearing hunger, thirst and heat, thin and covered with veins, he worshipped the god Sharva, reciting the eternal Brahman."}},{"n":13,"text":"भक्तानुकम्पी भगवांस्तस्य चक्रे ततो दयाम् ।\nस्वप्नान्तेऽप्यथ चैवाह हरः सिन्धुपतेः सुतम् ।\nवरं वृणीष्व प्रीतोऽस्मि जयद्रथ किमिच्छसि ॥","meaning":{"en":"The blessed Hara, kind to devotees, then took pity on him; at the end of a dream he spoke to the Sindhu king's son: \"Choose a boon, Jayadratha. I am pleased; what do you wish?\""}},{"n":14,"text":"एवमुक्तस्तु शर्वेण सिन्धुराजो जयद्रथः ।\nउवाच प्रणतो रुद्रं प्राञ्जलिर्नियतात्मवान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"So addressed by Sharva, Jayadratha, the Sindhu king, bowed to Rudra with folded hands, composed."}},{"n":15,"text":"पाण्डवेयानहं संख्ये भीमवीर्यपराक्रमान् ।\nएको रणे धारयेयं समस्तानिति भारत ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"May I alone in battle hold back all the Pandavas, of Bhima's might and prowess,\" he said, O Bharata."}},{"n":16,"text":"एवमुक्तस्तु देवेशो जयद्रथमथाब्रवीत् ।\nददामि ते वरं सौम्य विना पार्थं धनंजयम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Thus addressed, the lord of the gods said to Jayadratha: \"I give you the boon, gentle one, except for Partha Dhananjaya.\""}},{"n":17,"text":"धारयिष्यसि संग्रामे चतुरः पाण्डुनन्दनान् ।\nएवमस्त्विति देवेशमुक्त्वाबुध्यत पार्थिवः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"You will hold back four of Pandu's sons in battle.\" Saying to the lord of gods, \"So be it,\" the king awoke."}},{"n":18,"text":"स तेन वरदानेन दिव्येनास्त्रबलेन च ।\nएकः संधारयामास पाण्डवानामनीकिनीम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"By that boon and by the power of his divine weapon he alone held back the Pandava army."}},{"n":19,"text":"तस्य ज्यातलघोषेण क्षत्रियान्भयमाविशत् ।\nपरांस्तु तव सैन्यस्य हर्षः परमकोऽभवत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"At the sound of his bowstring on his palm, fear entered the Kshatriyas, and a supreme joy came to your army's enemies."}},{"n":20,"text":"दृष्ट्वा तु क्षत्रिया भारं सैन्धवे सर्वमर्पितम् ।\nउत्क्रुश्याभ्यद्रवन्राजन्येन यौधिष्ठिरं बलम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing the whole burden laid on the Sindhu king, the Kshatriyas, shouting, rushed, O king, where Yudhishthira's army was."}}]}]}